{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bundle","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use a bundle to name a set of components that often go together, such as everything a ship"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"needs, so you can spawn them in one step and keep that set in one place. Declare the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bundle’s contents in its "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Bundle\/body-9bv1p","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" property. The body is built by "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/BundleBuilder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", so you"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can list components and other bundles, and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"if"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"switch"},{"type":"text","text":" and optional values:"}]},{"code":["struct Armor: Component { var rating: Int }","","struct Ship: Bundle {","    var position: Position","    var armored: Bool","","    var body: some Bundle {","        position","        Velocity(dx: 0, dy: 0)","        if armored { Armor(rating: 10) }","    }","}","","var world = World()","let ship = world.spawn(Ship(position: Position(x: 0, y: 0), armored: true))","print(world.contains(Armor.self, in: ship))","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Removing a bundle type removes every component type the bundle can hold, including the types"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of branches that weren’t taken:"}]},{"code":["var world = World()","let ship = world.spawn(","    Ship(position: Position(x: 0, y: 0), armored: false),","    Health(current: 50)",")","","world.remove(Ship.self, from: ship)","print(world.contains(Position.self, in: ship), world.contains(Health.self, in: ship))","\/\/ Prints \"false true\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Component","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a bundle of itself, so anywhere a bundle is expected, you can pass a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"single component."}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Foundation also declares a type named ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bundle"},{"text":". In a file that imports Foundation,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"write ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ECS.Bundle"},{"text":" to name this protocol.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Note","style":"note"}]}],"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"inheritsFrom","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Inherits From","kind":"relationships"},{"type":"inheritedBy","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Component"],"title":"Inherited By","kind":"relationships"},{"type":"conformingTypes","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Disabled","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/EitherBundle","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Swift\/Never","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Swift\/Optional","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Prefab","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Targets","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/docum